cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ai-patterns in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ai-patterns: A pattern library for AI products that act"
abstract: >-
  An open research project on how user experience changes as AI moves from
  answering to acting, and a pattern library for the interactions that don't
  have established conventions yet. Each pattern is observed in a shipping
  product, written down as a portable UX contract (anatomy, behavior,
  accessibility, content guidelines) separate from its implementation, and
  organised by the job it does for the user: start, ask, steer, oversee,
  trust or recover. The catalogue is readable by people and by agents
  (Markdown, JSON, MCP and a Claude Code skill).
authors:
  - given-names: Carlos
    family-names: March
repository-code: "https://github.com/carlosmarch/ai-patterns"
url: "https://ai-patterns.app"
license: MIT
